req('SQL-03','Immutable identity, state vocabulary and UTC','individual source owner; platform coordinates','Before-write checks and FK/enum/check constraints','Primary and owning FK identities cannot be reassigned. Every mapped FK uses RESTRICT for key update/deletion; Privacy must act explicitly. Mutable source revision advances exactly once through compare-and-swap. Generation/fence cannot decrease. Time intervals require end > start; supported states are source-specific. Enum existence never authorizes a legacy/deferred transition. UTC instants use timestamptz(6); local availability separately carries IANA timezone.','Authorized source update increments expected revision and preserves identity','Stale competing revision, negative generation, swapped owner or invalid interval denied')
