req('SQL-07','Scoped idempotency and economic effects','platform mechanism; effect meaning remains owner','Compound unique constraints and durable fingerprint/result receipts','Command identity is (ownerModuleId,operation,subjectScope,semanticKey). Economic effect identity is separately (ownerModuleId,operation,subjectScope,semanticEffectKey); inbox identity is (consumerOwner,handlerName,outboxMessageId). Every duplicate preserves the original fingerprint/result; changed fingerprint conflicts. Per-source ledger semanticEffectKey plus typed effectReceiptId binds actual owner/currency/source. Permanent business effects must not depend on short transport retention.','Identical replay yields original receipt; different owners/scopes can use their own equal textual key','Same scoped key with changed fingerprint or duplicate money/points/usage source effect rejected')
req('SQL-08','Atomic source, owner history and outbox','each source owner + platform integration','Server-stamped transaction IDs and per-source deferred constraint triggers','All candidate rows have mutationTransactionId stamped by PostgreSQL; caller spoofing rejected. For each registered source mutation, concrete table/PK/revision and owning command receipt must match an OwnerMutationEvidence record in the same transaction. Required domain history and finite registered event/command intents must also match that transaction/source revision. Each source-specific trigger is generated from this ledger after approval, uses fixed identifiers and SECURITY INVOKER; no generic source repository/dynamic caller SQL. For Customer creation require CustomerProfileLifecycleEvent plus customer.lifecycle_changed.v1 and assignDefaultFreeTrack.v1 command intent. Nonmutating resolve/replay emits no duplicate source effect. Owner evidence JSON is closed under contracts/database-review/owner-mutation-evidence.v1.schema.json; private text/credentials never copied wholesale.','Commit source/history/receipt/outbox together; rollback any part leaves none','Missing evidence/required intent, foreign owner/revision, forged transaction ID or precommitted reused proof rejects at COMMIT')
req('SQL-09','Fencing, reclaim and truthful reservation release','platform mechanism with source semantic receipts','Row locking + lease compare-and-swap + deferred effect/receipt checks','Work claim serializes by work ID; each claim/reclaim strictly increases fence. Completion/effect writes require current fence and lease identity. Inbox/effect commits share source transaction. Reservation quantity > 0. Deadline expiry alone never establishes noncommit; release after unknown requires matching durable fenced_noncommit receipt preventing late source commit. Unknown remains reserved/reconcile-required. Delivery may repeat, business effect may not.','Current worker commits once; valid new-fence reclaim resumes after crash; explicit noncommit safely releases','Old worker completion/effect, deadline-only release, double claim at same fence or duplicate effect denied',models=['RuntimeWorkItem','RuntimeAttempt','RuntimeInboxReceipt','RuntimeEffectReceipt','RuntimeReservation','TrackUsageReservation','OrderSessionReservation'])
req('SQL-10','Order source/participant and purchased-scope coherence','transaction_order','CHECK plus deferred source-family/participant constraint trigger','Offering source: offeringId nonnull, gigAssignmentId null, seller nonnull, no screening child. Gig source: offeringId null, gigAssignmentId nonnull, seller nonnull, no screening child. Screening source: both marketplace refs null, seller null and exactly one OrderScreeningSource. Self-paid screening subjectUserId equals buyerUserId and its selected Candidate/Professional profile belongs to that User; no sponsored flow. Order/customer/user, Offering seller and accepted Gig winner must match. Buyer/customer required for all new Orders/Booking/holds/locks. Immutable purchase revisions and named purchased units retain price/fees/currency/title/scope/quantity/version; no repricing from current catalog.','One coherent Offering, accepted Gig or approved conditional self-paid screening source can be represented','Zero/multiple sources, fake screening seller, wrong package/subject/buyer/seller or duplicate Gig conversion rejected',stage='LATER_ORDERED_COMMERCE_SLICE',models=['Order','OrderScreeningSource','OrderPurchaseRevision','OrderPurchasedUnit','GigAssignment','Booking','BookingHold','BookingSlotLock'])
req('SQL-11','Agreement execution and Payment-owned outcomes','transaction_order and payment_payout_tax','Immutable revisions + coherent references + unique effects','Signature/electronic consent/document executionRevisionId belongs to its Agreement and same Order purchase revision. Document hash/object version matches actual immutable bytes and signer role. Never infer signature from legacy URL/hash/cache. PaymentEffect purchaseRevision/order/currency/amount/operation must match its frozen owner instruction and runtime effect identity; payout/ledger/corrections preserve original lineage. Tax liability is an explicit reviewed policy input, not the historical default.','Matching execution signature/document or authorized Payment receipt can be retained','Cross-agreement document/signature, altered finalized purchase, mismatched effect/currency or unapproved tax default rejected',stage='LATER_ORDERED_COMMERCE_SLICE',models=['Agreement','AgreementExecutionRevision','AgreementSignature','AgreementDocumentSnapshot','AgreementElectronicConsent','PaymentEffect','ProfessionalBalanceLedgerEntry','PayoutTransfer','SalesTaxCalculation','SalesTaxTransaction'])
req('SQL-12','Typed Track selection, Free/paid and UTC usage','track_subscription_entitlement','Subject XOR/coherence triggers, unique current selection and atomic reservations','Exactly one typed profile FK matches AccountTrack and each profile.userId equals row.userId; plan/grant definition track/value kind matches. TrackBaseSelection unique(userId,track). Free enrollment is provider=none under a free plan, no provider customer/subscription identity. Immutable enrolled policy version; current paid-through selection cannot be overwritten by delayed Free. TrackUsageEvent acceptedAt determines UTC period; counter equals retained usage/corrections, not authoritative reset state. Reservation and consumed source identity unique; unavailable/unknown never allows quota or releases it.','Correct Free enrollment replays; current paid selection survives delayed Free; same UTC-period usage survives plan switch','Wrong actor-profile/track, multiple current bases, paid downgrade, typed-value mismatch, duplicate usage or destructive reset denied',models=[r['model'] for r in rows if r['source_owner']=='track_subscription_entitlement'])
req('SQL-13','Purchased units, interval exclusivity and provider currentness','transaction_order / booking_calendar / job_interview / video_session','Deferred coherence + native GiST exclusion + generation checks','OrderSessionReservation unit belongs to purchase and matching Booking Order; reserved/committed quantity cannot exceed that frozen purchased unit. Select a native GiST exclusion over (professional_profile_id WITH =, tstzrange(starts_at,ends_at,\'[)\') WITH &&) for lock status active/converted, using btree_gist. Verify and separately authorize that extension before the later scheduling migration; it is not installed by this review or required by F0. Release/expiry is an explicit fenced owner transition, not a clock-only predicate. Authoritative hold relation is BookingSlotLock.bookingHoldId. Booking/Interview successor cannot branch/cycle; parent Application/Organization/Candidate and audiences coherent. CalendarDesiredMapping has exactly one parent and applies only matching parent/audience/desired generation. Video room credentials are not persisted as reusable join URLs.','Two nonoverlapping valid locks and matching current provider mapping work','Overlapping racing locks, wrong purchased unit, stale callback, cross-Application Interview, branched successor and stale-room credential denied',stage='LATER_SCHEDULING_SLICE',models=['OrderSessionReservation','OrderPurchasedUnit','BookingSlotLock','BookingHold','Booking','JobInterview','JobInterviewParticipant','CalendarDesiredMapping','BookingVideoRoom','JobInterviewVideoRoom'])
req('SQL-14','Privacy generations, actual receipts and exact export accounting','privacy_data_erasure plus actual source executors','Typed descriptor uniqueness, receipt coherence and generation/tombstone checks','Each instruction is unique request/owner/target-kind/source/action/generation and binds exact source/field-map/executor version. Receipt generation and instruction match. retained requires approved legalBasisRef, omitted requires owner reason/accounting; unknown/failed cannot complete request. Export-ready requires all owner accounting, exact immutable Media object version/size/digest and complete manifest bound to same generation. Restore markers reapply erasure/restriction generation before serving restored data. Deadlines originate at statutory request event, not reset by verification.','Current completed/retained/omitted accounting forms a truthful nonproduction result; supported exact export bytes match manifest','Old-generation completion, accepted-as-completed, missing owner, assumed backup purge or mismatched export bytes rejected',models=[r['model'] for r in rows if r['source_owner']=='privacy_data_erasure'])
