req('SQL-16','Non-authorizing projections, evidence schemas and monetary invariants','each canonical source owner','Field classification, typed evidence schemas and owner-specific invariant triggers','Compatibility/display/projection fields listed per model cannot authorize a source action. All new required storage identities/constraints live in normalized columns, not JSON. Every Json field is enumerated in database-candidate-json-boundaries.json. Initial F0 accepts only the exact registered evidence/result/outbox shapes; other F0 metadata and JSON-valued entitlements stay null. Deferred nullable fields deny nonnull values and deferred nonnullable fields block their table migration until an exact closed schema is reviewed. Every Json field remains private and requires its exact registered closed schema/version and owner serializer before its owning stage activates; it never supplies actor authority, implicit provider approval, lifecycle success or economic identity. JSON evidence allowed field set is generated from the reviewed per-model schema and excludes raw personal bodies/secrets. Signed points/balance/correction ledgers preserve sign; ordinary prices/quantities and fees obey source policy nonnegative bounds. No invented blanket monetary cap, refund timer or legal period.','Authorized owner can append coherent signed correction and rebuild a projection without changing source truth','Projection-based permission, arbitrary JSON keys, implicit legal/provider result, malformed price/interval or unsigned invalid ledger correction denied')
